# ROLES: the session-to-role ledger (machine-read; copy to .team/roles)
#
# One row per session id that may author a gate row or a commit. The role guards read
# this file, not roles.md (that is the prose definition of each role):
#   - gate-check: a PASS whose author is NOT listed here fails CLOSED once this file exists
#     (an unverifiable lens), and a PASS by a `manager` is always refused.
#   - pre-commit-role / deny-manager-code-write: a session whose role is `manager` cannot
#     commit or write application code.
#   - self-test: reports FIX when this file is missing or the current session's role does
#     not resolve.
# `enforcement/new-session --role <role> <session> <branch>` appends the row for you.
# Roles: manager | architect | researcher | developer | security | reviewer | qa
#
# Format: `session | role`. A leading table pipe is tolerated; blank and # lines ignored.

| session | role |
|---|---|
| manager-1 (EXAMPLE) | manager |
| dev-a (EXAMPLE) | developer |
| reviewer-1 (EXAMPLE) | reviewer |
| security-1 (EXAMPLE) | security |
| qa-1 (EXAMPLE) | qa |
